Z||000003||Cooter||11-29-2000||07:36 PM||||My uncle almost became road kill to a deer last week. He hit the deer with his car and it came smashing through the windshield and into the front seat! The deer hooked its antlers behind Doug's jaw on his right side and nearly ripped his lower jaw off. When the paramedics found him, they thought he was dead. The deer was- it turns out that during the struggle, Doug was able to grab its antlers and twist until he broke the deer's neck. Almost gave a new meaning to the term "road kill".||||reg||1
