Z||000011||jlhuber||11-30-2000||01:11 AM||||I hit a deer with my '86 GT.  55mph and it did about $2500 in damage, damn whitetails.  Killed the deer on impact, (upon gutting it, found a broke rib had pierced the heart and other organs) threw it up into the air about 6 feet.  (that deer was f*#$ed up)  While the deer was in the air, I had to look UP THROUGH the t-tops to see the deer.  I thought for sure that it was going to land on top and mess up my 'tops.  The deer ended up 25 feet down the road from where I had hit it, wrapped around a 6 inch round tree in the ditch.  Thank god for full coverage insurance though.  The only visible damage was that my front fascia emblem was gone, the left turn indicator lens was cracked, and the left side marker light trim (black strip) was broke and hanging down.  The car was 100% driveable and all turn indicators worked.  The local GM dealer did a decent job on the repair.  Car came out of the shop looking better than it did before I hit the deer.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Spyder||11-30-2000||02:39 AM||||My little brother in law, Allen, who just turned nine, went hunting for the first time two weeks ago.  His father, Steve put him into a deer stand and gave him his gun.  Steve said that he needed to go back to his truck to get something and told young Allen to make sure you don’t  take a shot until you see antlers and the body of the deer.  His father made it to his truck and at that time he heard a shot.  Scared him a little and decided to go quickly to check on Allen.  Then another shot, Steve was now running to check on Allen.  When Steve got to Allen, he was casually climbing down the tree stand, Steve, out of breath, asked “what are you doing?”.  Allen said “I’m getting down to get my deer.“.   Steve asked where his deer was at. Allen said one is over by the tree and the other is over yonder by  them bushes.   He had killed two bucks, and killed them both instantly. lol<P>I saw 8 deer on my way home from work last night.  <BR>Luckily none of them decided to commit suicide.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000013||hugh||11-30-2000||07:01 AM||||A few years ago my youngest son went to Elizabethtown college near Harrisburg,Pa.He hit one of three deer that ran out in front of his car.Messed up the sheetmetal,but didn't do any major damage.This happened just a mile from where a friend of his was killed by a deer the previous year.The deer was hit by a car going the other direction and came through his windshield.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Wolfhound||11-30-2000||07:15 AM||||In a freak accident on HY 280 near Auburn, several years ago, a deer ran in front of a semi. The deer bent a tie rod on the truck, causing it to veer into an on coming car. Four in the car were killed. ||||reg||1
