Z||000018||Wolfhound||11-30-2000||03:31 PM||||frontal lobe<P>Yep, They are hunted heavily but have gotten to the point they are a constant hazard at night. If you are away from the city it,s very dangerous to drive over fourty.<P> What often happens is a deer will run across in front of someone and they will be watching it and never see the second following deer they hit.<P> A few weeks ago I drove into Notasulga (which is really a small town) and had a young doe run out in front of me, turn and run right through the middle of town. It was pretty comical. They aren't near as agile on pavement as in the woods. She looked as if she were running on ice. Kind of a SNL version of the lead in to Northern Lights.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 11-30-2000).]||||reg||1
